# RISC0 Metrics Standards

## Context
- Applied when implementing proof generation and monitoring
- Focuses on consistent metrics collection and emission
- Ensures proper tracking of proof performance
- See 2001-risc0-api for high-level RISC0 integration guidelines
- See 2003-risc0-receipts for proof handling details

## Requirements
- Collect and emit session statistics:
  - Track total cycles and cycle breakdowns
  - Monitor segment counts for multi-segment proofs
  - Record proof sizes (journal, seal)
  - Track seal and journal sizes for storage requirements
- Calculate cycle breakdowns:
  - User cycles: Application computation
  - Paging cycles: Memory management
  - Reserved cycles: System operations
  - Verify total cycles match component sum
- Track proof sizes and components:
  - Journal size metrics
  - Seal size for both Composite and Succinct receipts
  - Input and output digest sizes
  - Committed output sizes
- Use consistent metric names and labels:
  - Include receipt type in metrics
  - Label cycle types appropriately
  - Use consistent units (bytes, cycles)
  - Add context to metric events
- Implement proper error tracking:
  - Log proof generation failures
  - Track compression errors
  - Monitor verification failures
  - Record timing information

## Examples

<example>
// Good: Complete metrics collection
fn collect_proof_metrics(info: &ProveInfo, receipt: &Receipt) {
    // Track cycle counts
    emit_histogram!(MetricEvents::ProofCycles, info.stats.total_cycles as f64,
        system => "risc0",
        cycle_type => "total"
    );
    
    let user_cycles = info.stats.user_cycles;
    let paging_cycles = info.stats.paging_cycles;
    let reserved_cycles = info.stats.reserved_cycles;
    
    // Verify cycle counts
    debug_assert!(
        info.stats.total_cycles == user_cycles + paging_cycles + reserved_cycles,
        "Cycle counts don't add up"
    );
    
    // Emit component cycle counts
    emit_histogram!(MetricEvents::ProofCycles, user_cycles as f64,
        system => "risc0",
        cycle_type => "user"
    );
    
    // Track proof sizes
    emit_histogram!(MetricEvents::ProofSize, receipt.journal.bytes.len() as f64,
        system => "risc0",
        component => "journal"
    );
    
    // Handle different receipt types
    match &receipt.inner {
        InnerReceipt::Composite(cr) => {
            emit_histogram!(MetricEvents::ProofSize, cr.seal_size() as f64,
                system => "risc0",
                component => "seal",
                receipt_type => "composite"
            );
        }
        InnerReceipt::Succinct(sr) => {
            emit_histogram!(MetricEvents::ProofSize, sr.seal_size() as f64,
                system => "risc0",
                component => "seal",
                receipt_type => "succinct"
            );
        }
        _ => {
            error!("Unexpected receipt type");
        }
    }
}
</example>

<example>
// Good: Timed operation tracking
fn process_proof(receipt: Receipt) -> Result<Vec<u8>> {
    emit_event_with_duration!(MetricEvents::ProofProcessing, {
        // Process the proof
        let result = process_inner(&receipt)?;
        Ok(result)
    }, receipt_type => receipt.inner.type_name())
}
</example>

